message.content:
I can see the vulnerability. In `mg_mqtt_next_prop`:

```c
uint8_t *i = (uint8_t *) msg->dgram.buf + msg->props_start + ofs;
uint8_t *end = (uint8_t *) msg->dgram.buf + msg->dgram.len;
size_t new_pos = ofs, len;
prop->id = i[0];  // <-- READ 1 happens HERE before any bounds check!

if (ofs >= msg->dgram.len || ofs >= msg->props_start + msg->props_size || (i + 1) >= end)
  return 0;
```

The `prop->id = i[0];` reads from `i` BEFORE the bounds check. If `ofs` is large enough that `i` points past the end of the buffer, this is a heap-buffer-overflow READ of 1 byte.

Now let me find the fuzz harness to understand how the input is structured.

